          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "4.2 Decimal Multiplication"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.279,
            0.849,
            0.339
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example 1:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Arshad goes to a stationery shop and purchases 5 pens. If one pen costs ₹9.5 (9 rupees and 50 paisa), how much should he pay the shopkeeper?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.353,
            0.495,
            0.376
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "What operation must we use here?"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.379,
            0.827,
            0.424
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We have to multiply 9.5 by 5, which is the same as adding 9.5, 5 times. That is "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "9.5 \\times 5 = 9.5 + 9.5 + 9.5 + 9.5 + 9.5 = 47.5."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.428,
            0.846,
            0.467
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We can also directly multiply the numbers by converting them into fractions."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.468,
            0.463,
            0.504
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "9.5 is "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 9 5 } { 1 0 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and 5 is "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 5 } { 1 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " as a fraction."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.508,
            0.418,
            0.545
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The cost of 5 pens "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "= { \\frac { 5 } { 1 } }   \\times   { \\frac { 9 5 } { 1 0 } }"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.548,
            0.846,
            0.587
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Recall that, to find the product of two fractions, we multiply the numerators and multiply the denominators."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.421,
            0.586,
            0.572,
            0.687
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_2_equation_11.jpg",
          "content": "\\frac{5}{1} \\times \\frac{95}{10} = \\frac{5 \\times 95}{1 \\times 10} = \\frac{475}{10} = 47.5"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.692,
            0.41,
            0.712
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The cost of 5 pens is ₹47.5."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.721,
            0.846,
            0.787
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example 2:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " A car travels 12.5 km per litre of petrol. What is the distance covered with 7.5 litres of petrol? We have to multiply 12.5 by 7.5."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.791,
            0.498,
            0.81
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The distance covered = 12.5 × 7.5"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.334,
            0.816,
            0.665,
            0.854
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_2_equation_15.jpg",
          "content": "\\frac{125}{10} \\times \\frac{75}{10} = \\frac{125 \\times 75}{10 \\times 10} = \\frac{9375}{100} = 93.75"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.86,
            0.481,
            0.879
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The distance covered is 93.75 km."
            }
          ]
        },
